{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/593524-do-you-add-the-supernatural-tolerance-to-the-vs-roll-on-embeds","id":593524,"title":"Do you add the Supernatural Tolerance to the vs roll on embeds.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T21:35:40-07:00","id":593524,"title":"Do you add the Supernatural Tolerance to the vs roll on embeds.","content":"I know that with exploits you do, but what about the embed, also what page does it say that. I can't seem to find it saying that in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6959-brandong13","name":"brandong13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:42:38-07:00","id":593546,"title":"","content":"There's actually a sidebar in the book (I don't have it on me, I'm not at home) discussing whether Embeds actually need a resistance (which is subtractive, not a contested roll) <i>at all</i>. But typically any Embed that can be defeated will be resisted by of the resistance traits (Resolve/Composure/Stamina) from the Embed roll rather than being a contested roll.<br /> <br /> If the situation requires a contested roll, there's always Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:45:26-07:00","id":593549,"title":"","content":"For an example of an Embed that does provoke a contested roll, you can look at No Quarter on p. 130, which does include Supernatural Tolerance in its contesting pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:56:31-07:00","id":593558,"title":"","content":"Doesn't seem to always be the case though. I looked it up on the index, and there are six embeds that have contested rolls:<br /> Apple of Dischord: Vs. Integrity (Flowers 93)<br /> No Quarter, as mentioned<br /> Call Out: Vs. Presence + ST (Flowers 97)<br /> Associate and Integrate: Vs. Resolve + Composure (Flowers 100)<br /> Clothes Make the Man: Vs. Wits + Chosen Skill (Flowers 101)<br /> Wave Function Collapse: Vs. Stamina + ST (Flowers 104)<br /> <br /> So, the answer is still... &quot;depends&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T02:13:48-07:00","id":593643,"title":"","content":"Wow thx you guys, this helps a lot. but where is the table for if it does or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6959-brandong13","user":"brandong13","date":". 07-17-2015, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6959-brandong13","name":"brandong13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:37:13-07:00","id":594836,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider - The vast majority of Embeds don't work on supernaturals at all. Well, demons anyways, but if we extrapolate that to include angels and other game lines, then it makes things far less crazy than you'd think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}